  "description": "Life's Too Good is the debut studio album by Icelandic alternative rock band the Sugarcubes. It was released 25 April 1988 by One Little Indian in the UK and Europe and in May 1988 by Elektra Records in the US. The album was an unexpected success and brought international attention for the band, especially to lead singer Björk, who would launch a successful solo career in 1993.",
